<title>UK: Central European Media sets dollar, mark bonds.</title>
<headline>Central European Media sets dollar, mark bonds.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following two bonds were announced by lead manager Morgan Stanley, Dean Witter, Discover &amp; Co.</p>
<p> BORROWER   CENTRAL EUROPEAN MEDIA ENTERPRISES LTD</p>
<p>* * *</p>
<p> AMT    $100 MLN	COUPON     9.3875    MATURITY  * 15.AUG.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.909    PAY DATE    20.AUG.97</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 REOFFER    99.909    SPREAD	+312.5 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	B1	  S&amp;P	  B+	  YIELD	 9.405 PCT</p>
<p> NOTES   * NON-CALL FOUR</p>
<p>* * * *</p>
<p> AMT    140 MLN DEM   COUPON     8.125     MATURITY    15.AUG.04</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  99.520    PAY DATE    20.AUG.97</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 REOFFER    99.520    SPREAD	+312.5 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	B1	  S&amp;P	  B+	  YIELD	 8.216 S/A</p>
<p> NOTES   * NON-CALL FOUR. SEC REGISTERED</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
